    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Valid Parentheses\n\nGiven a string s containing just the characters '()', '{}' and '[]', determine if the input string is valid: open brackets must be closed by the same type in the correct order, and every close bracket has a matching open.\n\nExample: s = '([{}])' -> true; s = '(]' -> false.\nConstraints: 1 <= len(s) <= 10^4.",
      "id": "m-0",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-11T10:00:37.037Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Edge cases to cover before submitting: empty input, single element, and the all-duplicates case.\n\nComplexity check: one pass, O(n) time, O(n) auxiliary space for the map. That meets the constraint.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-11T10:00:37.333Z",
      "durationMs": 14481,
      "stepIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "commentary",
